    {
      "id": "e78a9ab0e1c9b80542982bb86a05632b3ea7cc40",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 492102688,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Thanks Gerald! I noticed the failed pipelines ever since my https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/1651 got merged but was not able to figure out what was the problem. \n\nWith this change the errors are now visible. The link errors I think can be solved by including dot11decrypt_util.c unconditionally. Like this:\n\n```\ndiff --git a/epan/crypt/CMakeLists.txt b/epan/crypt/CMakeLists.txt\nindex d350ee41c8..df4e989a4a 100644\n--- a/epan/crypt/CMakeLists.txt\n+++ b/epan/crypt/CMakeLists.txt\n@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@ set(CRYPT_HEADER_FILES\n \n set(CRYPT_FILES\n        dot11decrypt.c\n+       dot11decrypt_util.c\n        dot11decrypt_tkip.c\n        ${CUSTOM_CRYPT_SRC}\n )\n@@ -40,7 +41,6 @@ if (GCRYPT_VERSION VERSION_LESS 1.6.0)\n else()\n        list(APPEND CRYPT_FILES\n                dot11decrypt_ccmp.c\n-               dot11decrypt_util.c\n                dot11decrypt_gcmp.c\n        )\n endif()\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 361322,
            "username": "mikaelkanstrup",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Mikael Kanstrup",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6c2a0d80250f78d0aedbde71226698ae3da909955086967b6027583b9c614e2e?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/mikaelkanstrup"
          },
